Z||000015||BluByYou||12-23-1999||07:30 AM||||Monkey got it all straightened out.  I was talking about Chris Moore.  He lives up the road from me, less than a mile.  I don't know the Chris from Indy.  Chris Moore & I are in Auburn, Indiana.  Regarding the question about Fieros at the auction .... Usually, that's not the place to go for a Fiero.  I saw a really customized (mural, funky paint, etc) for $13,000.00.  A bit high, I thought.  Chris has thrown a shin-dig for the last 3 or 4 years over the Labor Day weekend.  I had posted an invititation about 2 weeks before and didn't get a single response  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">.  Anyway, we had some nice cars show up, and I DO have pics.  What I don't have is a scanner.  I need to get some other things scanned, so I'll make a point to get the pics up in here.||||reg||3
Z||000016||88 Database Nut||12-23-1999||08:45 AM||||Just wanted you Indiana Boys to know that it does my poor transplanted heart good to see so many nice Fiero Guys in my Favorite state.<BR>I grew up in Fort Wayne, but didn't even know what a Fiero was until I moved to Atlanta.  Are any of you first owners, and if so what dealer did you get it from?<P>I must be homesick, 'cause reading all those old familiar town names makes me want to jump in the Fiero and visit y'all.  Since I can't, I'm with you in spirit, and to ALL fiero fans everywhere, Happy Holidays!<P>John Willhoff, Fort Wayne '65, Purdue '88||||reg||7
Z||000017||BluByYou||12-23-1999||01:39 PM||||'88 DatabaseNut:<BR>Ah .... Ft. Wayne.  My class ring says Northrop High School - sound familiar?  I say "my ring says that" because I actually graduated from a town I'd rather not reveal.  Anyway, I can only speak for Chris and myself in saying that there aren't any original owners here.  Interestingly enough, I am the second owner and still have the "Bostwick Pontiac" sitcker in the lower driver side of the windshield.  They didn't use todays "bumper stickers" to advertise, which makes it something I like to point out at shows.||||reg||6
Z||000018||Monkeyman||12-26-1999||06:36 PM||||BBY--Maybe we graduated from the same HS.  I graduated from Logansport State Hospital HS.  What about you? <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  Just kidding although I probably should have graduated from there.  <P>88 Nut--If you're planning a trip back here let me know.  I can get you a good deal on a motel.  But bring your Fiero, 'cause Wabash won't take any ricers.  (Supposed to be AmerEx, but...well, you know how I am! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">)<P>Damn, it's good to be back.  I'll never be gone 4 days at a time again.  This really is a drug.  ||||reg||1
